      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: Thanks for the workaround advice - I did this already (well, something similar - I used Blend to Shape to apply it to basis) and it works as a workaround.  That still does not explain this regression with 1088 though.  Model makers often make models with many shape keys to allow people to buy the model and customize the appearance without needing any Blender knowledge.  If this is intended behavior from the VRchat developers, they need to document it.",
