      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue has caused problems for me too. My avatar's breast size shape key was set to 75 by default and I had an FX layer that would reducethat size to 45 for a different outfit. Despite that animation not being active, just having it exist seemed to set my breast size to 100 and cause them to clip through my clothes. \nIt seems to happen any time a nonzero default blendshape value gets modified by an animation in an fx layer even if that animation is not playing. Strangely this behavior was often times not observed by me, I only became aware of it after someone asked me why my breasts were clipping. Some players would see my avatar correctly, some would see the clipping. Even stranger than that though is the fact that sometimes my avatar would have the blendshape issue, but would look fine in a mirror (see screenshot)\nEdit: This behavior would happen regardless of whether or not I had \"write defaults\" enabled.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
