  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-06T16:01:19.342Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have an avatar with a blendshape on his body called \"Eyes_Pupils_Big_L\" and \"Eyes_Pupils_Big_R\" which makes his pupils bigger.  I upload it with a value of 40.  There is also on my FX layer a hand gesture controller that transitions from Any State into an animation that increases the value of that blendshape to 100 when GestureLeft = 4.  This is set up exactly as all of the tutorials and vrchat examples show, including with a transition back from Any State to Idle.  Starting with build 1088, when I load into the game my pupils appear to be set to 100 and not the 40 that I uploaded them with.  However, if I set them to 0 in Unity and re-upload, they are correctly set to 0 in the game.  If I delete the animation entirely from the FX layer, the problem is resolved as well.  However, if I keep the animation and create a condition that is impossible to achieve (such as GestureLeft = 20) the problem still happens.  It appears that 1: if the blendshape I uploaded the avatar with is substantially greater than 0 (40 in this case) and 2: there is an animation somewhere on the FX layer that adjusts this value to 100 even if it is never triggered, and 3: there is a gesture layer present at all (can be completely blank, doesn't matter, just has to exist and be set on the descriptor) then something happens where VRchat is incorrectly identifying the default state of that blendshape.  If I trigger that gesture and then go back to a different one, I can see my pupil start to shrink to the correct size before springing back to 100.  If I upload the avatar with the pupil big blendshape set to 0 instead of 40, everything works as intended and there are no issues.  This was working fine before build 1088.",
